        "UpdatedIso"    : "2026-10-30T14:58:00.000Z",
        "CreatedBy"     : "USR00000001",
        "UpdatedBy"     : "USR00000001",
        "Description"   : "ValeVision AURA's scene for one project (the 'aura file'), schema 1.0.0 (05__Contracts__JsonSchemas/AuraRender__Schema__AuraScene__1.0.0__.json in AURA's app folder; the rules: AuraRender__SCHEMA__AuraScene__.md). Written by the AURA API into <project>/ValeVision__AuraRender/UserData__AuraScene/<id>__AuraScene__.json: the import (method one copies ValeVision 3D's whitecard GLBs into Content__AuraScene__ModelFiles), a re-import (the replaced set zipped into its 00__Archive, one zip kept), and each library asset stored the first time it is placed (its MOD .glb and DAT .json into Content__AuraScene__AssetFiles, instanced where it can be). User data: written on the server, collected to the PC, never pushed, never web-served; every save keeps the previous copy in ProjectData__Revisions. Placed assets and given materials are the drawing set's (AuraDrawingSet__Engine.Settings.Assets and .Materials); a material's #Id is Object__Id here. World metres are the engine's: +Y up, the front of the building facing +Z.",
        "Note"          : "Abridged from Thrower, the first AURA scene (63403__Thrower: 7 model files, 17 objects; built 30-Oct-2026, no assets placed yet). Here: 5 model files, objects 1 to 5 (4 and 5 are two instances of one column shape, Object__Mesh 1), and 2 stored assets to show the record: one instanced (the bench) and one that grows its own shape each placement (the oak)."
    },
